  "koregaon-park": [
    "Across Koregaon Park, wedding venues range from compact family halls to larger destination-style properties, and the safa tying plan changes with the scale of the venue. Smaller, more intimate functions usually need a shorter, tighter schedule with the groom styled first and the rest of the group following quickly after. Larger multi-hall or multi-day venues need a longer plan, sometimes spanning more than one function in the same property, and we treat each function as its own booking within the same visit. Local venues in Koregaon Park are generally easy to access, which keeps setup time short, but properties further from the main area may need an earlier arrival buffer. We recommend sharing the venue name and rough guest count as early as possible, even before the date is fully locked, so we can flag any availability concerns during peak wedding weeks. If the celebration includes more than one ceremony — a haldi, a sangeet, the main wedding — let us know all the dates together so the Koregaon Park team can plan artist availability across the full run rather than one date at a time.",
    "For Koregaon Park weddings, the package decision is really a headcount decision first and a style decision second. Once we know how many people need styling — the groom, close family, and the wider baraat if applicable — we can recommend artist numbers and a realistic tying window. Families sometimes assume a bigger package is always safer, but an accurately sized package based on your actual guest list is usually more cost-effective and easier to schedule than an oversized one. If you're unsure of the final numbers this early, a rough range is enough to start the conversation; we'll confirm the exact count closer to the date. Multi-function weddings in Koregaon Park — where the same family books a haldi, sangeet and wedding day styling — often benefit from a combined package rather than three separate bookings, since it keeps pricing and artist scheduling consistent across all three events. If your celebration includes destination elements, such as a portion of the wedding happening outside Koregaon Park itself, mention that upfront too, since it changes how the package and travel logistics are structured.",
  ],
  "kalyani-nagar": [
    "Kalyani Nagar sees weddings across a mix of settings — banquet halls, hotel lawns, rooftop venues and home courtyards — and each one changes how the tying schedule is planned. A hotel booking usually means a fixed preparation room and predictable access, while a home or courtyard function often needs the team to adapt around family rituals happening in parallel. We ask about the venue type early so the right number of artists and the right pace are set from the start, rather than guessing on the day. Peak wedding months in and around Kalyani Nagar bring tighter artist availability, so dates during the busiest weeks benefit from earlier confirmation. Off-season and weekday bookings tend to have more flexibility on timing and can sometimes accommodate later confirmations. Either way, the core planning stays the same: confirm the property, the room being used for styling, and roughly how many people need to be ready before the first ritual or the baraat departure. Weather is a smaller factor for most Kalyani Nagar bookings since safa tying happens indoors or under cover, but for any outdoor portrait session immediately after styling, we factor in extra time so fabric and finishing hold up under natural light.",
    "Picking the right package for a Kalyani Nagar wedding usually comes down to three numbers: how many people need a safa, how much time is available before the ceremony, and how detailed the groom's own styling needs to be. A groom-only booking is the simplest option and works well for smaller functions or when family members already have their own arrangements. A groom-plus-family package adds a coordinated look for parents and siblings without the scale of a full baraati booking. The complete package — groom, family and baraat — is the most common choice for larger Kalyani Nagar weddings, since it keeps the whole wedding party visually consistent in photographs and keeps the tying schedule managed by one team rather than several. Fabric quality is a separate decision from group size: some families choose a premium fabric for the groom and a simpler, more economical option for the wider baraat, which keeps costs sensible without compromising the groom's look. Whichever package you're considering, sharing your rough budget alongside the guest count helps us recommend something realistic rather than the largest available option by default. We're happy to talk through two or three package options before you decide.",
  ],
